  "period_end": "2026-02-28",
  "title": "More ways to make and move media",
  "summary": "February widened the creative API while making community apps, model choices, and everyday account controls easier to navigate.\n\nAudio gained speech, transcription, and music endpoints; video gained LTX-2 and better image inputs and sizing. A new upload API gave generated work a place to put its files, while Seedream 5 and Nano Banana 2 expanded image options.\n\nCommunity submissions filled the catalog with creative tools, bots, learning apps, and developer utilities. Platform badges, clearer filters, and better descriptions made that growing collection easier to browse; the Community page gained a browsable Build Diary.\n\nPlay gained copyable request URLs, the API reference gained task-based examples and a video route, and OpenClaw got setup guidance and search options. The npm tools took new names, while Polly gained a chat-completions endpoint.\n\nClaude Opus and Sonnet moved to 4.6, GLM moved to GLM-5, and Gemini Pro and MiniMax received upgrades. Routing, aliases, and model listings were adjusted alongside them so clients have clearer choices.",
  "pr_count": 212,
